  "releaseNotes": "BREAKING (STK-15416): a 2xx response the client cannot parse now throws ApiException (ErrorCode 500, raw body in ErrorContent) instead of returning null. Void operations (the generated no-body DELETE/PUT calls) and binary responses (Stream, byte[]) are exempt and still return normally. If your code treats a null API result as not-found logic, review before upgrading. Also: enrollment status \"inactive\" (OneRoster v1.1 s4.13.8, deprecated) now deserializes to StatusEnum.Tobedeleted instead of failing. Numeric status values (e.g. \"status\": 1) now throw where they previously parsed leniently. Only the ENROLLMENT status enum accepts \"inactive\"; the other generated status enums are unchanged. Transport-level failures (DNS, connection refused, timeout) on typed calls now surface as ApiException (error code 500) instead of a null result. Serializing an EnrollmentType whose Status was never set now throws JsonSerializationException instead of silently writing the integer 0.",
